Recommends: tmux
Description: MaluOS office setup: the Business OS configuration interview for Claude Code
 The Claude Code plugin that configures a freshly installed MaluOS office
 (the server that runs the MaluDB Business OS kernel) after first boot:
 the deployment topology, the business domain and the first
 administrator, the re-provision, the office's names and the proxy's
 server blocks, the first sign-in hand-off, the provider keys through a
 protected prompt, the VM guest agent and one topology-aware summary.
 .
 The plugin is installed under /usr/share/maluos/claude-plugins with a
 local marketplace beside it, a sudoers rule that lets members of sudo
 run exactly its scripts as root without a password (Claude Code's shell
 cannot answer a prompt), and the launcher maluos-office-setup. `maluctl
 office-setup` installs Claude Code for the operator (Anthropic's native
 installer, per user) and starts the interview; `maluctl office-setup
 check` and `providers` run the plugin's scripts without Claude.
